{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"5300000000000001","type":"group","x":0,"y":500,"width":2050,"height":1150,"color":"5","label":"01 目标与市场指标 · Objectives and market measures"},
		{"id":"5300000000000002","type":"group","x":0,"y":1900,"width":2050,"height":1150,"color":"5","label":"02 交易与结算 · Transactions and settlement"},
		{"id":"5300000000000003","type":"group","x":0,"y":3300,"width":2050,"height":1150,"color":"5","label":"03 准备金框架 · Reserve frameworks"},
		{"id":"5300000000000004","type":"group","x":0,"y":4700,"width":2050,"height":1150,"color":"4","label":"04 下限与资产购买 · Lower bound and asset purchases"},
		{"id":"5300000000000005","type":"group","x":0,"y":6100,"width":2050,"height":1150,"color":"4","label":"05 利率与合同 · Rates and contracts"},
		{"id":"5300000000000006","type":"group","x":2450,"y":500,"width":2050,"height":1150,"color":"4","label":"06 银行、财富与抵押 · Banks, wealth and collateral"},
		{"id":"5300000000000007","type":"group","x":2450,"y":1900,"width":2050,"height":1150,"color":"4","label":"07 对外价格与需求 · External prices and demand"},
		{"id":"5300000000000008","type":"group","x":2450,"y":3300,"width":2050,"height":1150,"color":"6","label":"08 规则与可信性 · Rules and credibility"},
		{"id":"5300000000000009","type":"group","x":2450,"y":4700,"width":2050,"height":1150,"color":"6","label":"09 指引与供给权衡 · Guidance and supply trade-offs"},
		{"id":"530000000000000a","type":"group","x":2450,"y":6100,"width":2050,"height":1150,"color":"2","label":"10 公告与因果 · Announcements and causality"},
		{"id":"5300000000000000","type":"text","x":0,"y":0,"width":4500,"height":320,"text":"# 货币政策：实施 → 传导 → 可信预期 → 因果判断\n\n左栏 01–05：从目标、交易和准备金框架走到融资价格；右栏 06–10：从家庭与银行的反应走到政策规则、沟通和识别。按编号阅读，缩放后沿短箭头查看条件；跨区桥把同一知识对象连回整条路径。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nRead 01–05 down the left column, then 06–10 down the right. Follow implementation into financing, spending, expectations and causal inference. Arrows state conditional relationships; bridge cards connect sections through shared objects.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n连续阅读：[[02_Economy/03_货币银行学/16_货币政策的实施与传导|货币政策的实施与传导]]"},
		{"id":"5300000000002001","type":"text","x":100,"y":600,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### [[货币政策]]\n\n央行通过金融工具影响金融条件，以实现制度规定的政策目标。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nMonetary policy uses financial instruments to influence conditions in pursuit of its mandate.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001001","type":"text","x":850,"y":600,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### [[货币政策操作目标]]\n\n日常直接引导的市场变量，区别于最终的通胀和就业结果。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nAn operating target is a near-term market variable, distinct from ultimate inflation and employment outcomes.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001003","type":"text","x":1600,"y":600,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### [[央行管理利率]]\n\n央行直接规定合格账户或操作的回报，提供市场外部选择。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nAdministered rates set eligible account or facility returns, creating outside options for market participants.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001002","type":"text","x":100,"y":1200,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### [[联邦基金利率]]\n\n美国特定无担保短期融资市场的成交利率，不是所有贷款利率。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nThe federal funds rate prices a specific U.S. unsecured funding market, not every loan.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001014","type":"text","x":850,"y":1200,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### [[有效联邦基金利率]]\n\n申报隔夜交易的成交量加权中位数，区别于单笔价格和目标中点。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nEFFR is the volume-weighted median of reported overnight trades, not a single price or target midpoint.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001004","type":"text","x":100,"y":2000,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### [[公开市场操作]]\n\n央行进行买断、卖断或临时证券交易；用途须结合操作目标判断。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nOpen-market operations trade securities outright or temporarily; their role depends on the operating objective.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001005","type":"text","x":850,"y":2000,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### [[回购协议]]\n\n先出售资产，再按约定条件购回等价资产，形成两条现金腿。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nA repo combines an initial asset sale with an agreed repurchase of equivalent assets.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001006","type":"text","x":1600,"y":2000,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### [[央行回购方向]]\n\n先看谁支付现金，再核对机构的 repo／reverse repo 命名。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nEstablish who pays cash, then check the institution's repo and reverse-repo terminology.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000002002","type":"text","x":100,"y":2600,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### [[央行准备金余额]]\n\n合格机构的央行账户资产，对应央行负债；不同于公众银行存款。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nReserve balances are eligible institutions' assets and central-bank liabilities, distinct from public bank deposits.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000002003","type":"text","x":850,"y":2600,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### [[央行购债结算链]]\n\n银行与非银行卖方产生不同存款分录；沿实际账户追踪结算。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nBank and non-bank sellers generate different deposit entries. Trace the actual credited accounts.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000003001","type":"text","x":1600,"y":2600,"width":350,"height":350,"text":"### 结算之后，才问传导\n\n准备金变化要结合[[准备金数量与政策立场|操作背景]]；价格作用要查[[资产购买的组合再平衡|资产替代]]；支出反应再看[[利率渠道]]。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nSettlement alone identifies neither stance nor spending. Check implementation, asset substitution and behavioural responses separately.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001007","type":"text","x":100,"y":3400,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### [[利率走廊]]\n\n合格存借便利给出上下参照；稀缺区间可用准备金数量引导利率。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nEligible deposit and lending options bracket rates; reserve quantities can steer trading on downward-sloping demand.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001008","type":"text","x":850,"y":3400,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### [[充足准备金框架]]\n\n需求近乎平坦时，主要用管理利率引导市场，小幅数量变化作用有限。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nOn near-flat reserve demand, administered rates do most of the steering and modest quantity changes matter little.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001010","type":"text","x":1600,"y":3400,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"2","text":"### [[管理利率的市场边界]]\n\n准入、抵押、污名与中介成本使名义便利不成为人人可用的硬界。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nAccess, collateral, stigma and intermediation costs qualify apparently strict administered-rate bounds.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001009","type":"text","x":850,"y":4000,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"2","text":"### [[准备金数量与政策立场]]\n\n补充结算余额可能维持原目标；准备金不变时仍可调整利率立场。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nReserve replenishment can preserve an unchanged target; rate conditions can change without reserve drainage.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001013","type":"text","x":100,"y":4800,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### [[有效利率下限]]\n\n现金替代和金融传导限制降息空间；实际约束并不统一等于零。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nCash substitution and financial transmission limit rate cuts; the effective bound is not universally zero.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001011","type":"text","x":850,"y":4800,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### [[量化宽松]]\n\n用新创造的央行货币购买大规模资产，意在放松金融条件。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nQE finances large-scale asset purchases with newly created central-bank money to ease financial conditions.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001012","type":"text","x":1600,"y":4800,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### [[资产购买的组合再平衡]]\n\n资产不完全替代时，私人风险供给改变可推动组合、价格与收益率调整。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nImperfect substitution lets changed private risk supply induce portfolio, price and yield adjustments.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000002004","type":"text","x":850,"y":5400,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"2","text":"### [[QE 与贷款创造|QE 的贷款边界]]\n\n准备金增加不把贷款按固定倍数放大；贷款仍受需求与银行约束。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nQE-created reserves do not multiply lending mechanically. Credit demand and bank constraints still matter.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000002005","type":"text","x":1600,"y":5400,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### 长期收益率的两个对象\n\n分别打开[[未来短率预期]]与[[期限溢价]]。预期路径和风险供给可同时改变，分解需要模型。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nSeparate expected short rates from the term premium. Both expectations and risk supply can change; decomposition requires a model.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001020","type":"text","x":100,"y":6200,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### [[事前实际利率]]\n\n同期限近似为名义利率减预期通胀；精确随机期望须逐状态换算。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nThe same-horizon approximation subtracts expected inflation from the nominal rate; exact stochastic expectations require state-by-state conversion.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001021","type":"text","x":850,"y":6200,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### [[利率渠道]]\n\n实际储蓄回报和融资机会成本改变消费投资选择，反应取决于约束。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nReal saving returns and financing opportunity costs affect spending choices, conditional on preferences and constraints.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001022","type":"text","x":1600,"y":6200,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### [[合同重定价与政策传导]]\n\n重置决定账单何时变；固定合同下仍可能提前调整消费或转移风险。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nRepricing dates the bill change. Fixed contracts still allow anticipatory spending responses and shifted rate exposure.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001023","type":"text","x":1600,"y":6800,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### [[现金流再分配渠道]]\n\n利息收付相抵，不保证消费反应相抵；要看收付方各自的支出倾向。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nOffsetting interest receipts and payments need not offset in consumption when spending responses differ.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000003002","type":"text","x":100,"y":6800,"width":350,"height":350,"text":"### 当前合同与未来路径\n\n[[前瞻指引]]可先改变[[未来短率预期]]。当前账单、未来融资、银行供给是不同环节；续读右栏 06。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nGuidance can change expected future rates before bills reprice. Current contracts, future funding and bank supply are distinct; continue at 06.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000002006","type":"text","x":2550,"y":600,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### [[政策传导的估值渠道|政策如何进入估值]]\n\n先拆预期现金流与所需回报，再算净价格变化；宽松不保证股价上涨。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nSeparate expected cash flows and required returns before valuing the net effect. Easing need not raise equities.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001025","type":"text","x":3300,"y":600,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### [[财富渠道]]\n\n资产价值改变终身可消费资源；持有人、负债与偏好决定消费反应。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nAsset values change lifetime consumable resources; ownership, liabilities and preferences shape the spending response.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001026","type":"text","x":4050,"y":600,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### [[财富效应与抵押效应]]\n\n愿意消费多少与能够融资多少是两条链；额度增加还不是实际借款。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nDesired consumption and available secured finance are distinct. More borrowing capacity is not an actual loan.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001024","type":"text","x":2550,"y":1200,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### [[银行贷款渠道]]\n\n银行自身资金成本、利润与资本改变贷款供给；区别于借款需求变化。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nBanks' funding, profits and capital can alter loan supply, distinct from changes in borrowing demand.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000002007","type":"text","x":4050,"y":1200,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### [[金融加速器]]\n\n借款人净值与抵押品通过融资条件反馈放大冲击；不是银行自身资本机制。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nBorrower net worth and collateral amplify shocks through financing feedback, distinct from banks' own capital mechanism.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001027","type":"text","x":2550,"y":2000,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### [[汇率传递]]\n\n给定汇率变化，先查进口边境价，再查零售价与价格篮子；幅度可不同。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nGiven an exchange-rate change, trace border prices, retail prices and the consumer basket separately.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001028","type":"text","x":3300,"y":2000,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### [[汇率与支出切换]]\n\n相对价格与产品替代改变贸易数量；数量反应不等于贸易金额必改善。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nRelative prices and substitutability affect trade volumes; the monetary trade balance need not improve.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000003003","type":"text","x":4050,"y":2000,"width":350,"height":350,"text":"### 从利率走到汇率\n\n先补海外政策、风险溢价与预期条件；再分开[[汇率传递|物价链]]与[[汇率与支出切换|需求链]]，不把加息固定配对为升值。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nCondition on foreign policy, premia and expectations. Then separate price pass-through from demand switching; a hike need not imply appreciation.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001040","type":"text","x":2550,"y":3400,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"6","text":"### [[泰勒规则]]\n\n把通胀偏离与产出缺口映射到名义政策利率；系数和输入口径须明确。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nThe Taylor rule maps inflation and output gaps into a nominal rate, with explicit coefficients and measurement choices.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001041","type":"text","x":3300,"y":3400,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"6","text":"### [[泰勒原则]]\n\n对持续通胀作超过一比一的名义响应；整体稳定仍取决于模型条件。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nRespond more than one-for-one to persistent inflation; economy-wide stability still depends on the model.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000002008","type":"text","x":4050,"y":3400,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"6","text":"### [[承诺与可信性]]\n\n在私人行动前可观察地改变续局博弈，再检查兑现承诺是否最优。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nChange the continuation game observably before private decisions, then check whether following through is optimal.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001042","type":"text","x":2550,"y":4000,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"6","text":"### [[政策时间不一致]]\n\n无新消息且目标、已知结构不变，私人选择既定后，事前计划失去续局最优性。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nWith no new information and unchanged objectives and known structure, an ex-ante plan ceases to be optimal after private choices are fixed.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001043","type":"text","x":3300,"y":4000,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"6","text":"### [[相机抉择的通胀偏差]]\n\n理性预期、直接控通胀且目标产出高于自然水平时，基准模型有通胀偏差。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nRational expectations, direct inflation control and an above-natural output target produce inflation bias in the benchmark model.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001044","type":"text","x":2550,"y":4800,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"6","text":"### [[前瞻指引]]\n\n沟通未来政策路径及条件，可能改变今天的融资与支出判断。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nForward guidance communicates future policy and its conditions, potentially changing financing and spending today.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001045","type":"text","x":3300,"y":4800,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"6","text":"### [[预测式与承诺式指引]]\n\n解释预期反应，与约束未来选择不同；同一低利率消息可有不同含义。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nForecasting the policy reaction differs from constraining future choices. The same low-rate message can carry different meanings.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001046","type":"text","x":4050,"y":4800,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"6","text":"### [[指引门槛与触发条件]]\n\n维持政策的条件失效，不自动触发改策；历史门槛须读原有语境。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nFailure of a condition for maintaining policy does not automatically trigger a change. Read historical thresholds in context.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001047","type":"text","x":2550,"y":5400,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"6","text":"### [[通胀预期锚定]]\n\n中长期预期围绕可信目标、较少随短期消息漂移；与工资定价期限分开。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nAnchored medium- and long-run expectations remain near a credible target, distinct from pricing-contract horizons.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001048","type":"text","x":3300,"y":5400,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"6","text":"### [[供给冲击下的政策权衡]]\n\n同时判断持续性、二轮效应、实际收入、时滞与福利基准，不能统一处方。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nAssess persistence, second-round effects, real income, lags and the welfare benchmark; no single response fits every supply shock.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000002009","type":"text","x":2550,"y":6200,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"2","text":"### [[意外信息定价]]\n\n先把公告与事前已知预期比较；结果的绝对水平不是价格反应基准。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nCompare the announcement with prior expectations; its absolute level is not the benchmark for a price response.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000003004","type":"text","x":3300,"y":6200,"width":350,"height":350,"text":"### 把整条路径用于一次决定\n\n沿[[02_Economy/03_货币银行学/16_货币政策的实施与传导#10. 贯通应用：读懂一次利率决定|贯通应用]]，逐项核对实施、合同、预期和反事实。一个家庭多付的利息，不是全经济消费损失。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nApply implementation, contract, expectation and counterfactual checks together. One household's higher interest bill is not the aggregate consumption loss.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001029","type":"text","x":2550,"y":6800,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"2","text":"### [[货币政策冲击识别]]\n\n分开央行对经济的内生反应与外生政策变化；窄窗口仍需识别假设。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nSeparate endogenous policy responses from exogenous variation. Narrow announcement windows still require identifying assumptions.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"5300000000001030","type":"text","x":3300,"y":6800,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"2","text":"### [[货币政策公告的信息效应]]\n\n同一公告可混合政策变化与经济判断；利率股价同向不是纯信息证明。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nOne announcement can mix policy and economic assessments. Joint rate-equity movements do not prove a pure information shock.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"}
	],
	"edges":[
		{"id":"5300000000004001","fromNode":"5300000000002001","fromSide":"right","toNode":"5300000000001001","toSide":"left","label":"目标转成可操作变量"},
		{"id":"5300000000004002","fromNode":"5300000000001001","fromSide":"right","toNode":"5300000000001003","toSide":"left","label":"由工具实施"},
		{"id":"5300000000004003","fromNode":"5300000000001002","fromSide":"right","toNode":"5300000000001014","toSide":"left","label":"汇总隔夜成交"},
		{"id":"5300000000004004","fromNode":"5300000000001001","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"5300000000001014","toSide":"top","label":"美国隔夜目标的监测"},
		{"id":"5300000000004005","fromNode":"5300000000001004","fromSide":"right","toNode":"5300000000001005","toSide":"left","label":"一种临时交易形式"},
		{"id":"5300000000004006","fromNode":"5300000000001005","fromSide":"right","toNode":"5300000000001006","toSide":"left","label":"依现金流辨方向"},
